      "heading": "B — Audience",
      "learner_facing": false,
      "markdown": "## B — Audience, Section Eight Signals and markings\n\nThe audience is first-time, never-licensed applicants preparing for the West Virginia Class E knowledge examination, reading at a plain-English level with no prior driving knowledge assumed. Section Eight teaches what each signal color, arrow, flasher and painted line requires of the driver. It depends on the traffic signs chapter for the stop and yield shapes and on the definitions chapter for right-of-way. The rules progress from railroad crossings, through steady and flashing signals and lane signals, to pedestrian signals and pavement markings.\n",
